      "statement": "On Windows, restrictDirToCurrentUser enforces owner-only intent with icacls by granting full control to the current user and the SYSTEM SID (*S-1-5-18) then removing inherited ACEs, because fs.chmod only toggles the read-only attribute on Windows; it is best-effort (returns false instead of throwing) and a no-op on non-Windows platforms.",
      "evidence": [
